{"id": "q-m01", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.785030300001381, "cost_usd": 0.0075575, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1949, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1205, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1067}, "total_tokens": 3154}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Look for half-grown or fully grown caterpillars. They are easiest to identify. [S1] Young larvae are pale. They become brown to pale green, then darker. [S1] Look for 3 yellow stripes on the back. Then look for a black stripe, then a yellow stripe on the side. [S1] Look for four dark spots forming a square on the second to last segment. Each spot has a short bristle. [S1] [S3] The head is dark. It has a pale upside down Y-shaped marking on the front. [S3]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m02", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.673372399993241, "cost_usd": 0.00678375, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1840, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1055, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 994}, "total_tokens": 2895}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Eggs are pale green or white at first. They get covered in scales. They turn clear brown to brown before hatching [S2]. They hatch in 2-3 days [S2][S1][S4].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m03", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.1280580000020564, "cost_usd": 0.0046865, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2039, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 503, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 459}, "total_tokens": 2542}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "The moth is 3 to 4 cm wide. Its front wings are dark brown. Its rear wings are grey white. [S2]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m04", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.236129900004016, "cost_usd": 0.00656825, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1960, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 969, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 909}, "total_tokens": 2929}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Look on the underside of the leaves near the base of the plant, close to where the leaf meets the stem [S2]. When numbers are high, eggs may be higher up or on nearby plants [S2].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m05", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.7241617999970913, "cost_usd": 0.0064225, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1789, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 985, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 928}, "total_tokens": 2774}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "They are called windows. They are caused by young Fall Armyworm caterpillars feeding on the undersides of leaves. [S3] Early instars cause windowing and shot holes. [S4]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [3, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m06", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.151293899994926, "cost_usd": 0.00638325, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1965, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 924, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 862}, "total_tokens": 2889}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "It is likely frass from Fall Armyworm. Frass is caterpillar poo. When it dries it resembles sawdust [S2] and has a sawdust-like appearance in the whorl [S5].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 5], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m07", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.645447399991099, "cost_usd": 0.00631, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2039, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 885, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 839}, "total_tokens": 2924}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "They eat each other. When larger they become cannibalistic to reduce competition for food [S1]. Larger larvae will eat smaller ones [S2].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m08", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 2.9876370999991195, "cost_usd": 0.00590225, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1961, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 812, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 745}, "total_tokens": 2773}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Under warm conditions, one female can lay 6 to 10 egg masses of 100 to 300 eggs each. This gives a maximum of 1 500 to 2 000 eggs in her lifetime of 2-3 weeks [S2].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m09", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "error": "Spark call failed: HTTP 400: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"content_policy_violation\",\"message\":\"The response was filtered due to the prompt triggering our content management policy.\",\"param\":\"prompt\",\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}", "correct": false, "latency_s": 3.4447752999985823}
{"id": "q-m10", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 5.045068499995978, "cost_usd": 0.00983075, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1748, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1799, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1704}, "total_tokens": 3547}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Fall armyworm makes windowing and shot holes on leaves [S1]. It causes defoliation in the whorl with fresh frass [S1]. It does not cause dead heart [S1]. Stem borers hide in the stems [S2]. They make a hole to bore and feed inside the stem [S1]. They cause deadheart in young maize plants [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 2, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m11", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 16.39154419999977, "cost_usd": 0.021813, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1688, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 4636, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 4548}, "total_tokens": 6324}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "The guide describes Sesamia calamistis [S6] and maize stem borer Busseola fusca in South Africa [S4]. Stem borer damage is compared with FAW damage [S5] [S6]. Stem borers do not leave big holes like FAW [S6]. They cause dead heart in young maize [S6].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [4, 5, 6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 2, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m12", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.1950939999951515, "cost_usd": 0.00518025, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2128, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 593, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 503}, "total_tokens": 2721}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "They are closely related, but have different behaviors and ecologies [S1]. Fall Armyworm rarely masses and marches across fields [S1]. African Armyworm is native to Africa and faces natural enemies like predators, parasitoids, and diseases [S1]. Fall Armyworm probably arrived in Africa without its natural enemies, so its numbers can grow unchecked [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m13", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "error": "Spark call failed: HTTP 400: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"content_policy_violation\",\"message\":\"The response was filtered due to the prompt triggering our content management policy.\",\"param\":\"prompt\",\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}", "correct": false, "latency_s": 3.4249505000043428}
{"id": "q-m14", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 4.760931299999356, "cost_usd": 0.00863625, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2183, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1390, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1338}, "total_tokens": 3573}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not say if FAW can be wiped out from Africa. Please contact your local extension officer. The moth can fly up to 100 km per night [S2].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m15", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 2.9506025000009686, "cost_usd": 0.00586135, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2063, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 798, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 762}, "total_tokens": 2861}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "The moth can fly up to 100 km in one night. [S1] [S4]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m16", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.680784800002584, "cost_usd": 0.00851235, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1984, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1445, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1374}, "total_tokens": 3429}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "You may not lose your whole harvest. FAW usually eats tender, young maize leaves in the whorl [S5] [S6]. Maize plants can significantly recover from early leaf damage [S1]. Attack on ears is rarer than leaf feeding [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 5, 6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "damage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m17", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 7.984474099997897, "cost_usd": 0.01418685, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2107, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 2744, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 2647}, "total_tokens": 4851}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Damage is most serious in the whorl. Stages 3 to 6 reach the whorl and make ragged holes in leaves [S4]. Young plants can lose the growing point and make no new leaves or cobs [S4]. Older plants with cobs can have kernels eaten [S4]. Maize can make up for leaf damage at early seedling or vegetative stage [S3].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [3, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "damage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m18", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 2.658048500001314, "cost_usd": 0.0054335, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2317, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 597, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 558}, "total_tokens": 2914}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. Heavy rains can wash young larvae off leaves, and drown those in the whorl. [S6]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "damage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m19", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.333364400008577, "cost_usd": 0.006744, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1951, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1013, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 942}, "total_tokens": 2964}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "No. Young maize can recover from early leaf damage [S4]. Leaf damage may not mean yield loss [S1]. Spraying is not a must when you see early defoliation [S1]. Early spraying kills natural enemies and may not be economical [S6].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 4, 6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "damage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m20", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 5.264300299997558, "cost_usd": 0.007681100000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2033, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1235, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1194}, "total_tokens": 3268}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The guides do not explain if planting date changes fall armyworm in maize. Please contact your local extension officer. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "prevent", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 2, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m21", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "error": "Spark call failed: HTTP 400: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"content_policy_violation\",\"message\":\"The response was filtered due to the prompt triggering our content management policy.\",\"param\":\"prompt\",\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}", "correct": false, "latency_s": 3.027552100000321}
{"id": "q-m22", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.851028699995368, "cost_usd": 0.0069645, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2158, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1004, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 915}, "total_tokens": 3162}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. In Brazil, chemical fertilizer gave higher FAW infestation than organic fertilizer (manure) or no fertilizer [S1]. Fertilizer type can change larval growth, larval death, natural enemies, and infestation level [S1]. You can compare no fertilizer vs chemical vs manure and check infestation, natural enemies, and yield [S1].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "prevent", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m23", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.679222899998422, "cost_usd": 0.00994525, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1860, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1793, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1683}, "total_tokens": 3653}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. Farmers who plant maize with beans and squash have less pest attacks [S3]. Mixed crops confuse armyworm, so it lays fewer eggs on maize [S3]. Try intercropping maize with cassava, which is not a host plant of the FAW [S1]. Using intercropping can help reduce FAW infestation [S4]. Keep flowering weeds around the plot to feed natural enemies that control FAW [S1] [S2].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2, 3, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "prevent", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m24", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 4.1214880000043195, "cost_usd": 0.00676875, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1981, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1010, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 943}, "total_tokens": 2991}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "Keeping plant diversity on the farm reduces Fall Armyworm infestation and supports natural enemies [S4]. Maize intercropped with other crops can have less infestation [S4]. The passages do not name cassava. Contact your local extension officer for advice.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "prevent", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m25", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 8.38556989999779, "cost_usd": 0.013688, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2396, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 2516, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 2316}, "total_tokens": 4912}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Push-pull is a habitat management strategy for maize. [S2] It uses maize grown with Desmodium and Napier grass or Bracharia. [S2] Conventional push-pull is maize with Desmodium silver leaf and napier grass. [S2] Climate-smart push-pull is Desmodium Greenleaf and Bracharia. [S2] It appears effective against fall armyworm compared to growing maize alone. [S2] [S1] It can reduce oviposition and feeding. [S2] It is pesticide free. [S2] It conserves natural enemies and increases their abundance, diversity and activity. [S2] It also controls striga weeds. [S2] It improves soil fertility through nitrogen fixation. [S2] It offers valuable fodder. [S2] It can increase maize grain yield in East Africa and similar areas. [S1]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "prevent", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m26", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.953863500006264, "cost_usd": 0.00635785, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1906, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 961, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 897}, "total_tokens": 2867}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "It is the pull trap plant around the maize. It attracts stemborers and FAW to lay eggs on it. It does not allow larvae to develop on it due to poor nutrition, so very few larvae survive. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "prevent", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m27", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.274247700013802, "cost_usd": 0.007692, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2026, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1214, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1129}, "total_tokens": 3240}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. Use climate-smart push-pull. It combines Desmodium Greenleaf and Bracharia cv Mulato II [S1]. It is designed for dry and hot conditions [S1] [S2]. Brachiaria grass grows fast with less water [S1]. It tolerates dry conditions better than Napier grass [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "prevent", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m09", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "blocked": true, "blocked_reason": "Spark content filter declined the request: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"content_policy_violation\",\"message\":\"The response was filtered due to the prompt triggering our content management policy.\",\"param\":\"prompt\",\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}", "cost_usd": 0.0, "latency_s": 4.395482499996433, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The extension guides on this device don't cover this well enough for a safe answer. Please contact your local agricultural extension officer.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 2, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
