{"id": "q-m28", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.516213599999901, "cost_usd": 0.0101446, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1923, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1847, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1715}, "total_tokens": 3770}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "No. It is yet too early to draw conclusions on GM maize for fall armyworm [S1]. Bt maize can decrease damage, but fall armyworm in the Americas evolved resistance to some Bt maize [S1]. Current Bt maize in Africa is aimed at maize stem borer, not fall armyworm [S1] [S2]. High seed cost, lack of supply, and small farm size mean low probability of sustainable use by smallholders [S3] [S4]. Stem borers showed resistance within two years in South Africa [S3] [S5].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], "answerable": true, "qtype": "prevent", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m29", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.6735568000003695, "cost_usd": 0.0086185, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2587, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1267, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1180}, "total_tokens": 3854}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. Ants are often among the most important predators of FAW larvae and pupae [S4]. Ants have been seen attacking and killing FAW larvae in maize fields in Africa [S4]. Pesticides dramatically reduced the presence and effectiveness of ants [S4]. You can attract ants by applying water and sugar over plants [S2].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "biocontrol", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m30", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.398198100010632, "cost_usd": 0.010086, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1891, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1817, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1727}, "total_tokens": 3708}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Apply a solution of water and sugar with the pump over the plants. [S1] Apply lard or fish soup on your maize plants. [S2] Predatory ants are attracted to lard, oil, bits of fish parts, or sugar. [S3] Once on the maize plants, they also find and eat FAW larvae. [S3]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2, 3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "biocontrol", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m31", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 3.8907832999975653, "cost_usd": 0.007062, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2015, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1069, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1034}, "total_tokens": 3084}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not explain how birds help with fall armyworm. Please contact your local extension officer.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [], "answerable": true, "qtype": "biocontrol", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m32", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.105214199997135, "cost_usd": 0.00747, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1879, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1205, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1166}, "total_tokens": 3084}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "A virus likely killed them. Virus-killed larvae become soft and many hang from leaves [S1][S6].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "biocontrol", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m33", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.453755399998045, "cost_usd": 0.00715535, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1677, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1216, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1153}, "total_tokens": 2893}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Those stiff white caterpillars were likely killed by fungus [S6]. Fungal-killed larvae turn rigid and appear “frozen” on the leaves, eventually turning white or light green, as the fungal spores mature [S6].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "biocontrol", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m34", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "blocked": true, "blocked_reason": "Spark content filter declined the request: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"content_policy_violation\",\"message\":\"The response was filtered due to the prompt triggering our content management policy.\",\"param\":\"prompt\",\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}", "cost_usd": 0.0, "latency_s": 5.448699000000488, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The extension guides on this device don't cover this well enough for a safe answer. Please contact your local agricultural extension officer.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [], "answerable": true, "qtype": "biocontrol", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 3, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m35", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.119031199996243, "cost_usd": 0.00935825, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1999, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1614, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1483}, "total_tokens": 3613}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Do not spray chemical pesticides repeatedly. This reduces natural enemies. [S3] Avoid overuse of synthetic insecticides. [S2] Keep diverse boundaries with open flowers and shrubs for habitat and food for natural enemies. [S2] Keep trees or bird perches in or near fields to attract birds that eat FAW. [S2] If pesticides are needed, choose products compatible with biological control such as Bt. [S2] Use proper planting dates, fertilization, soil health and moisture management, and mechanical controls and botanicals from early growth. [S3]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "biocontrol", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m36", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 3.7767982999939704, "cost_usd": 0.0072835, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2250, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1052, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1014}, "total_tokens": 3302}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not say if biopesticides kill fast. Contact your local extension officer. [S3]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "biocontrol", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m37", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 3.2962125000049127, "cost_usd": 0.00636785, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1948, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 951, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 905}, "total_tokens": 2899}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Start 5 days after emergence. Check your field every week. Look at 50 plants in 5 stations of 10 plants. [S2]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "local", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m38", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.586788199987495, "cost_usd": 0.01154775, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1731, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 2208, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 2133}, "total_tokens": 3939}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. You can crush egg masses between your fingers before they hatch [S1]. Visit fields at least twice a week during heavy infestation [S1]. Egg masses take 2-3 days to hatch [S1]. Do not keep children from school to do this work [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "local", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m39", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.3054467999900226, "cost_usd": 0.00804885, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2011, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1328, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1224}, "total_tokens": 3339}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. Farmers put ash, sand, sawdust or dirt into whorls to control FAW larvae [S2]. Ash, sand and sawdust may desiccate young larvae [S2]. Sand is very abrasive and can scar insect larvae [S1]. Ash is also very alkaline [S1]. They often seem to work, especially when applied directly into the whorls of infested plants [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "local", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m40", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.6167124999919906, "cost_usd": 0.00678675, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1907, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1036, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 986}, "total_tokens": 2943}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. Some farmers report pouring water into the maize whorl to drown the larvae. [S1] You can try it under your local conditions. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "local", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m41", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.701939599995967, "cost_usd": 0.0097106, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2266, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1644, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1462}, "total_tokens": 3910}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Collect mature fruits of neem (Azadirachta indica), remove the flesh and dehusk the seeds [S1]. Grind 500g of neem seed kernel in a mill or pound [S1]. Mix the crushed neem seed with 10 lit of water or more [S1]. Allow the extract to stand for at least for 5 hours in a shady area [S1]. Filter the mixture to obtain the extract [S1]. Add soap or detergent as surfactant/emulsifying agents [S1]. Spray the neem extract on maize or other cereal crops [S1]. Indicatively, 6 to 8 Kgs for Neem kernel’s might be required to treat one hectare of maize crop [S3]. Neem extract can be retained for at least 3 to 6 days [S3].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "local", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 3, "facts_total": 3, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m42", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.6534908000030555, "cost_usd": 0.006650850000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1933, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1022, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 974}, "total_tokens": 2955}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Indicatively, 6 to 8 Kgs for Neem kernel’s might be required to treat one hectare of maize crop. [S1] [S2]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "local", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m43", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.863422599999467, "cost_usd": 0.00829035, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1956, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1401, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1333}, "total_tokens": 3357}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "No. Do not assume botanical pesticides are always harmless to humans and animals [S2]. Some can be highly toxic, such as tobacco leaf extract, containing nicotine [S2]. Take precautions to reduce risks when preparing and using local botanicals [S2].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "local", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m44", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.281488100008573, "cost_usd": 0.0095411, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1685, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1775, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1696}, "total_tokens": 3460}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "You can use mature fruits of neem (Azadirachta indica), Neem leaves, and Pyrethrum extract [S3]. Tobacco leaf extract is named too, but it is highly toxic [S1]. Rely on traditional knowledge about plant toxicity. Take precautions when preparing and using local botanicals [S1].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "local", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m45", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 5.579329200001666, "cost_usd": 0.008306850000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1891, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1424, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1358}, "total_tokens": 3315}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Enter your field at least once a week [S3]. Walk a letter “W”, covering the entire field [S6]. If plots were planted at different times, with different varieties, or with different conditions, sample each plot differently [S6].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [3, 6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "scouting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 2, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m46", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.97137750001275, "cost_usd": 0.00874025, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1780, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1533, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1462}, "total_tokens": 3313}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Count only plants with fresh leaf damage or fresh frass in the whorl [S1] [S2]. Do not count plants with damage to older leaves and no clear signs of current damage [S2]. You do not need to find the larva [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "scouting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m47", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.9086531000066316, "cost_usd": 0.00518985, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2029, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 650, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 613}, "total_tokens": 2679}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "52 percent are infested.", "removed_sentences": ["Double 26 to get 52 in 100 plants [S1]."], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "scouting", "invented_quantity": true, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m48", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 3.21537449999596, "cost_usd": 0.006991600000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2209, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1021, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 973}, "total_tokens": 3230}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not say how many plants to sample. They describe AESA as weekly field observation [S1][S5]. Please contact your local extension officer.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 5], "answerable": true, "qtype": "scouting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m49", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.000972099995124, "cost_usd": 0.00715185, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2344, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1019, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 949}, "total_tokens": 3363}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Pheromone traps are for monitoring FAW. They attract and trap male moths. You count them to know if FAW is present and if you need more scouting. [S1] They are not a way to control FAW. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "scouting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m50", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.158013699998264, "cost_usd": 0.00673285, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1849, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1066, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1013}, "total_tokens": 2915}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Hang the trap from a suspended pole or branch about 1.5 m above the ground [S1]. Use one trap for every 0.5–2 ha [S1].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "scouting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m51", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.4487179000134347, "cost_usd": 0.00651485, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2154, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 925, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 880}, "total_tokens": 3079}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Replace the lure every 3–6 weeks [S2]. Plan for about five lures per trap for one maize growing season [S2].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "scouting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m52", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.0395037999987835, "cost_usd": 0.00599635, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2273, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 768, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 733}, "total_tokens": 3041}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Check the trap two times per week. Count the FAW moths inside. [S6]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "scouting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m53", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.9286443000019062, "cost_usd": 0.0086596, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2129, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1437, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1350}, "total_tokens": 3566}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Do not rush to spray early when you see fall armyworm. Spraying early kills natural enemies and may not pay [S1]. Young maize can recover from early leaf damage, so spraying is not a must at that time [S4]. Spraying many times is often not cost effective and brings risks to people, animals and the environment [S3].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 3, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m54", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "blocked": true, "blocked_reason": "Spark content filter declined the request: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"content_policy_violation\",\"message\":\"The response was filtered due to the prompt triggering our content management policy.\",\"param\":\"prompt\",\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}", "cost_usd": 0.0, "latency_s": 8.392647600005148, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The extension guides on this device don't cover this well enough for a safe answer. Please contact your local agricultural extension officer.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m55", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 7.285294300003443, "cost_usd": 0.01091585, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2421, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1882, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1768}, "total_tokens": 4303}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Avoid pesticides labelled with red and yellow. [S2] Avoid highly hazardous pesticides on Fall Armyworm. [S1] [S2] These include Methomyl, Acephate, Cyfluthrin, Benfuracarb, Methyl parathion, Carbaryl, Endosulfan, Carbosulfan, Lindane, Chlorpyrifos, and Diazinon. [S2] They pose great concerns for human health and the environment. [S2]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m56", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.198370700003579, "cost_usd": 0.0097526, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1725, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1813, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1724}, "total_tokens": 3538}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Look for the active ingredient [S1]. It is the poison that works [S1]. Products have different commercial names [S1]. Look for instructions for use [S1]. Look for personal protective equipment requirements [S1]. Look for re-entry intervals [S1]. Look for first aid statements [S1]. Look for toxicity colour code [S1].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m57", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 7.004258100001607, "cost_usd": 0.010724850000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2037, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1950, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1857}, "total_tokens": 3987}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Red and yellow are toxicity colour codes on the label [S1]. Pesticides labelled with red and yellow should always be avoided, unless proper conditions of use can be ensured [S3]. Some pesticides are more toxic than others [S1]. High toxicity means highly hazardous to health and the environment [S1]. Consider blue and green colour coded low-risk products instead [S2].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2, 3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m58", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "blocked": true, "blocked_reason": "Spark content filter declined the request: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"content_policy_violation\",\"message\":\"The response was filtered due to the prompt triggering our content management policy.\",\"param\":\"prompt\",\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}", "cost_usd": 0.0, "latency_s": 4.782012299998314, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The extension guides on this device don't cover this well enough for a safe answer. Please contact your local agricultural extension officer.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m59", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 9.473040700002457, "cost_usd": 0.013516, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2527, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 2437, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 2393}, "total_tokens": 4964}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not give a pesticide name to use. They only say avoid highly hazardous pesticides. Contact your local extension officer. [S4]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 2, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m60", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 2.5629890999989584, "cost_usd": 0.0055196, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1946, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 752, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 691}, "total_tokens": 2698}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Often no. Once the FAW is down in the whorl, the insecticides must reach them there [S1]. Spraying with backpack sprayers without delivering material directly into the whorl is often ineffective [S1].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m61", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.020880700001726, "cost_usd": 0.006524, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1707, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1033, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 952}, "total_tokens": 2740}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Check the direction and velocity of the wind [S1]. If the wind is blowing hard, do not spray [S1][S3]. Never walk into the wind when spraying [S1][S2][S3]. Always walk at 90 degrees angle to the wind [S1][S2][S3].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2, 3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m62", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.6124148999952013, "cost_usd": 0.007110600000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1920, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1134, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1088}, "total_tokens": 3054}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Bathe with SOAP immediately after spraying. [S2] Wash hands thoroughly with soap and water after handling pesticides and especially before eating. [S1]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m63", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "blocked": true, "blocked_reason": "Spark content filter declined the request: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"content_policy_violation\",\"message\":\"The response was filtered due to the prompt triggering our content management policy.\",\"param\":\"prompt\",\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}", "cost_usd": 0.0, "latency_s": 7.660842099998263, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The extension guides on this device don't cover this well enough for a safe answer. Please contact your local agricultural extension officer.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m64", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.795855799995479, "cost_usd": 0.0083771, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2073, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1387, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1337}, "total_tokens": 3460}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not give a dose per knapsack. Read the instructions on the label. The dose differs from product to product [S4]. Contact your local extension officer.\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m65", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.247771499998635, "cost_usd": 0.01108985, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1802, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 2105, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1957}, "total_tokens": 3907}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "The Economic Threshold Level (ETL) helps decide whether a pesticide should be sprayed. [S2] It is the pest density where the cost of yield loss equals the cost of treatment. [S2] Spray only when justifiable. Low levels at some maize stages may not cause much yield loss. [S4] It is calculated from management costs, commodity price, and damage coefficient. [S2] If field counts are higher than the ETL, spraying was traditionally advised. [S2] ETL is useful but not the only analysis. Also check natural enemies, plant health, weather, health, and maize price. [S2]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 3, "facts_total": 3, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m66", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.4649283999897307, "cost_usd": 0.006523350000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1814, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1027, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 966}, "total_tokens": 2841}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Children and pregnant women are most at risk. They are particularly susceptible to adverse effects from exposure to pesticides [S2]. Pesticides might damage the unborn child (baby in the mother’s womb) [S3].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-m67", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.5643053999956464, "cost_usd": 0.0066935, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1727, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1067, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 996}, "total_tokens": 2794}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Acute effects appear promptly, or within 24-48 hours of exposure [S1]. Signs include headache, fatigue, nausea, vomiting and sweating [S1]. Signs also include irritation, swelling, respiratory difficulties, seizures, dizziness and increased heart rate [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "pesticide", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c01", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.615265700005693, "cost_usd": 0.00978785, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1964, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1751, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1678}, "total_tokens": 3715}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "This may be cassava mosaic disease. It shows clear green and yellow spots that grow bigger. Then leaves shrink and shrivel up. [S1] Check leaf underside with a magnifying glass, because green spidermite curling can look like mosaic. [S5]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 5], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c02", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.398329899995588, "cost_usd": 0.006841, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2100, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 992, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 920}, "total_tokens": 3092}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "It spreads mainly when you plant already infected cassava cuttings. [S1] In a small number of cases it spreads from plant to plant by whitefly. [S1] Use of diseased cuttings leads to immediate contamination of a newly planted field. [S6]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c03", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.6711878000060096, "cost_usd": 0.005839850000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2056, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 795, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 747}, "total_tokens": 2851}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "It can cause production losses of between 50 and 90 percent [S2]. A severe form caused yield losses of 80–100 percent [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c04", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 7.0865076999907615, "cost_usd": 0.010208100000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2052, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1824, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1728}, "total_tokens": 3876}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Use virus-free planting material [S6]. Infected cuttings give infected plants [S5]. The disease spreads mainly through planting already infected cuttings [S1]. Use resistant or tolerant varieties [S3] [S6]. Whitefly spreads the disease from plant to plant in a small number of cases [S1]. Harvesting leaves and taking cuttings can increase the severity [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 3, 5, 6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 2, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c05", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.308050899999216, "cost_usd": 0.0061306, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1969, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 889, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 825}, "total_tokens": 2858}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. Mosaic and brown streak do not pose problems for human health [S4]. You can still use roots with brown streak if the infection is not too severe [S2]. Clean the roots well before you process them [S2].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c06", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 7.279499099997338, "cost_usd": 0.010301, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1808, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1892, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1841}, "total_tokens": 3700}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not say where the first symptoms show. They say mosaic spreads by infected cuttings and by whitefly [S2]. Please contact your local extension officer for advice.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 0, "facts_total": 1, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c07", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.2869604999868898, "cost_usd": 0.005173100000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2036, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 644, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 608}, "total_tokens": 2680}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. Harvesting leaves and cassava cuttings can increase the severity of the disease [S2].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c08", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.458665300000575, "cost_usd": 0.00649585, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1809, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1022, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 983}, "total_tokens": 2831}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "This is cassava brown streak disease (CBSD). The roots have brown spots and streaks. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c09", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.976403099994059, "cost_usd": 0.005998, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1837, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 871, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 835}, "total_tokens": 2708}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "No. Symptoms on leaves are not very clear and often go undetected until harvest. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c10", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.079694500003825, "cost_usd": 0.00596875, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1987, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 820, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 769}, "total_tokens": 2807}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. The roots can still be used if the infection is not too severe. It takes a lot of time to clean the roots before they can be processed. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c11", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.621815999998944, "cost_usd": 0.007812600000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1720, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1358, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1258}, "total_tokens": 3078}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Phytosanitation means removing and destroying all diseased plants in your cassava field. [S1] It removes sources of contamination. [S1] This helps you get healthy planting material and a healthy crop. [S1] Check every single row. [S1] Remove every plant with disease symptoms without hesitation. [S1] It is the uprooting of diseased materials. [S4]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c12", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.335371299996041, "cost_usd": 0.00767125, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1853, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1260, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1202}, "total_tokens": 3113}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Do phytosanitation once a week for the first two months of the crop once the gaps have been filled. [S4] Then do it every two weeks until you harvest the cuttings. [S4]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c13", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.459287300007418, "cost_usd": 0.00679435, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1701, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1124, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1071}, "total_tokens": 2825}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Uproot and destroy the whole plant. Destroy all plants that have symptoms of disease. [S2] Localize, uproot and destroy all plants with symptoms. [S6]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c14", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.2673210999928415, "cost_usd": 0.00521, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1856, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 680, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 630}, "total_tokens": 2536}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "No. Do not go from your production field straight to the multiplication field to do phytosanitation. Avoid carrying diseased materials with you in the field. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
