{"id": "q-c20", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.890757300003315, "cost_usd": 0.00738225, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1887, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1182, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1141}, "total_tokens": 3069}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "The bacteria live in the plant's interior. That is why plant cuttings are the biggest source of contamination. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c21", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.230335400003241, "cost_usd": 0.0064796, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1813, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1017, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 972}, "total_tokens": 2830}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Anthracnose is a fungal disease. It begins with wounds from stings of an insect named Pseudotheraptus devastans. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c22", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.275696400000015, "cost_usd": 0.00740125, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1875, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1190, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1097}, "total_tokens": 3065}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Anthracnose is a fungal disease [S1]. Look for cankers (lesions) on the stem and at the base of the petioles of the leaves [S1]. Deep cankers reach the central part of the stem and the stem breaks easily [S1]. Leaves fall off and the stem dries up [S1]. Plant tops look dead [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c23", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.957240699994145, "cost_usd": 0.00625875, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1947, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 900, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 835}, "total_tokens": 2847}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Anthracnose blocks sap flow. Leaves fall off and stem dries up. Plant tops look dead [S2]. Bacterial blight also makes the upper part die back from high to low [S4]. So the two look the same.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 4], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c24", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.265846899987082, "cost_usd": 0.00556735, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1787, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 810, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 751}, "total_tokens": 2597}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Do not worry much. Leaf spots occur on old leaves and the economic impact is limited [S1]. There are three types caused by Cercosporiosis [S1]. Knowing this helps to avoid anxiety [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c25", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.454836799995974, "cost_usd": 0.00606235, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1877, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 900, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 853}, "total_tokens": 2777}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Leaf spots are caused by Cercosporiosis. [S1] There are three types. [S1] They occur on old leaves. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c26", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 8.784886199995526, "cost_usd": 0.00965785, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1979, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1716, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1645}, "total_tokens": 3695}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "This is likely cassava mealy bug. It shows as a white mass like white flour in the dry season. It covers the insect with its eggs inside. It can slow or stop growth and make growing points stunted and bushy. [S1] [S2]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c27", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.789191899995785, "cost_usd": 0.00619435, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1425, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1064, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 988}, "total_tokens": 2489}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "It was brought under control by research to introduce and release a parasitic wasp (Apoanagyris lopezi). [S1] The wasp lays its eggs in the mealy bug. [S1] Its larvae develop in the mealy bug and kill it. [S5]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 5], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c28", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.986366099998122, "cost_usd": 0.0061751, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1600, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1008, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 957}, "total_tokens": 2608}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "It appears mainly in the dry season [S1] [S2]. It goes away in the rainy season [S1]. The rain washes it off [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c29", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 9.05041219999839, "cost_usd": 0.010256600000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1421, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 2021, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1903}, "total_tokens": 3442}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Use resistant varieties [S2]. Plant at the beginning of the rainy season [S2]. Do good fertilization [S2]. Adopt improved cultural practices [S2]. Use biological control [S2]. The parasitic wasp (Apoanagyris lopezi) lays its eggs in the mealy bug [S5]. Its larvae develop in the mealy bug and kill it [S5]. It is efficient at keeping populations of cassava mealy bug in check in most situations [S5].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 5], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c30", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.258326499999384, "cost_usd": 0.00569575, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1840, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 799, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 748}, "total_tokens": 2639}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Eggs and young bugs travel by wind and rain. They also travel on cassava cuttings, animals and humans. This spreads them to other plants and fields. [S2]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c31", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.588433400000213, "cost_usd": 0.0053281000000000005, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1361, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 879, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 833}, "total_tokens": 2240}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Light attack causes malformation of the roots. Heavy attack stops root formation. Feeding holes can let pathogens enter and cause root rot. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c32", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.16843350000272, "cost_usd": 0.0057331000000000005, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1362, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 974, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 936}, "total_tokens": 2336}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "A small red ant. It lives with root scale. It is a good indicator of root scale [S2].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c33", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 8.889515400005621, "cost_usd": 0.0089976, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1359, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1743, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1680}, "total_tokens": 3102}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "There are no efficient ways to control root scale insects now [S1]. Rest the land for 3–5 years [S1]. Do deep soil preparation [S1]. This combined work can help reduce infestation [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 2, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c34", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 7.838292400003411, "cost_usd": 0.0086766, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2095, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1451, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1381}, "total_tokens": 3546}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Probably not mosaic. In dry season small spots and curling are easily confused with mosaic virus [S1]. Check underside of leaves with a magnifying glass for small green spidermites [S1]. Place them on white paper to see them [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c35", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.956665300007444, "cost_usd": 0.0065011, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1582, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1090, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1046}, "total_tokens": 2672}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Look on the underside of the leaves [S1] [S2]. Use a magnifying glass to see them easily [S2].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c36", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 7.539577999996254, "cost_usd": 0.008160800000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1880, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 227}, "output_tokens": 1426, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1329}, "total_tokens": 3306}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Look on the underside of leaves with a magnifying glass for small green mites [S5]. Sick leaves show small spots and curling [S5]. Use resistant varieties [S3]. Plant at the beginning of the rainy season [S3]. Do good fertilization [S3]. Do improved cultural practices [S3]. Use biological control using T. aripo as a predator [S3].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [3, 5], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c37", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 7.523440599994501, "cost_usd": 0.00822635, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1660, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1473, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1364}, "total_tokens": 3133}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "It lives on the underside of the leaves [S1]. It feeds on the leaves and destroys the plant's potential chlorophyll [S1]. It feeds by sucking and injects a toxin [S3]. Leaves show chlorosis as small spots and curling [S3]. Growth can slow down or halt [S1]. Internodes become shorter at the terminal parts [S1]. Strong infestations can lead to the dropping of young leaves [S3].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c38", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.519911700001103, "cost_usd": 0.0074076, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1668, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1278, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1199}, "total_tokens": 2946}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Find the hole or tunnel made by the mole rat [S1]. Place hot pepper, dry cow dung and cotton wool at the entrance to the tunnel [S1]. Burn them [S1]. Drive the smoke into the tunnel [S1]. This smoke is known to drive away the mole rat [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 3, "facts_total": 3, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c39", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 3.9629565000068396, "cost_usd": 0.00496285, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1674, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 701, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 665}, "total_tokens": 2375}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Mole rats can eat up to 50 percent of your cassava in the field. [S1]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "identify", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c40", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 9.306359599999269, "cost_usd": 0.0084226, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1834, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1468, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1417}, "total_tokens": 3302}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Yes. Hills to ridge up cassava plants gives satisfactory results in mole control [S1]. Test ridges, hills, and direct planting to adapt the method [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "manage", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c41", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": false, "latency_s": 7.939966299993102, "cost_usd": 0.00886335, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1646, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1627, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1515}, "total_tokens": 3273}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Use healthy cuttings. Diseased cuttings spread mosaic virus and brown streak virus and contaminate a new field. [S4] Use the hardened middle part of the stem. [S6] Throw away the top and bottom parts. [S6] Cut 15–25 cm long with at least 4–5 eyes. [S6] Avoid bruising or damage to the epidermis and buds. [S6] Avoid termite damage. [S6]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [4, 6], "answerable": true, "qtype": "planting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": false, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 2, "correct": false, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c42", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.425256700007594, "cost_usd": 0.0073346, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1936, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1182, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1109}, "total_tokens": 3118}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Farmers use sections 40–60 cm long. [S2] Ideally use hardened middle parts cut 15–25 cm long with a minimum of 4–5 eyes. [S2] For multiplication use 10–15 cm long with 3 eyes. [S3]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "planting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c43", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.747517800002242, "cost_usd": 0.0064321000000000005, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1911, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 977, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 931}, "total_tokens": 2888}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "You need 2,500 m of cuttings for 1 ha [S1]. Keep 5-10 percent extra for gaps [S1].\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "planting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c44", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 5.666146000003209, "cost_usd": 0.006976100000000001, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1860, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1120, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1066}, "total_tokens": 2980}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "No. Long-term storage of cassava stems is not possible because stems dehydrate [S1]. You can store cassava stems for several weeks if kept under the right conditions [S1].", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": true, "qtype": "planting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c45", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 6.103261099997326, "cost_usd": 0.00708425, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1805, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1136, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1098}, "total_tokens": 2941}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Use small cuttings with 3 eyes (or nodes), 10–15 cm long. [S3]\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "planting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 2, "facts_total": 2, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c46", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 7.940457900011097, "cost_usd": 0.00669735, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1858, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1055, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 991}, "total_tokens": 2913}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Too frequent harvesting of leaves can reduce root production. Each harvest may result in reduced root yield. Applied research advises 2–3 harvests of leaves at 2-month intervals, starting at least 4 months after planting. [S2]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2], "answerable": true, "qtype": "planting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 3, "facts_total": 3, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-c47", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": true, "latency_s": 4.25279959999898, "cost_usd": 0.0054381, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1857, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 759, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 727}, "total_tokens": 2616}, "supported": true, "answer_shown": "Keep the field ≥ 200 m from any cassava field. [S3]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [3], "answerable": true, "qtype": "planting", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": 1, "facts_total": 1, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-o01", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": null, "blocked": true, "blocked_reason": "Spark content filter declined the request: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"content_policy_violation\",\"message\":\"The response was filtered due to the prompt triggering our content management policy.\",\"param\":\"prompt\",\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\"}}", "cost_usd": 0.0, "latency_s": 8.25865609999164, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The extension guides on this device don't cover this well enough for a safe answer. Please contact your local agricultural extension officer.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [], "answerable": false, "qtype": "out_of_scope", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": null, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-o02", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": null, "latency_s": 7.619271000003209, "cost_usd": 0.00778135, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2103, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1238, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1182}, "total_tokens": 3341}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "These guides are about Fall Armyworm (Spodoptera frugiperda) [S3]. They do not give an insecticide for grasshoppers. Please contact your local extension officer for advice.\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [3], "answerable": false, "qtype": "out_of_scope", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": null, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-o03", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": null, "latency_s": 8.793773900004453, "cost_usd": 0.0088106, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1665, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1609, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1558}, "total_tokens": 3274}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages show fall armyworm damage [S4] and cassava leaf spots [S2], but no fungicide for northern leaf blight. Contact your local extension officer.\n\nSafety: if you use any pesticide, read and follow the product label exactly. Wear gloves, a mask, long sleeves and boots, keep children and animals away, never eat, drink or smoke while spraying, and wait the pre-harvest interval on the label before harvesting. Ask your extension officer if you are unsure.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 4], "answerable": false, "qtype": "out_of_scope", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": null, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-o04", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": null, "latency_s": 7.898507999998401, "cost_usd": 0.0076271, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1728, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1312, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1256}, "total_tokens": 3040}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not say how to treat storage bags for weevils. They only list storage pests and their management as a topic to learn [S1]. Please contact your local extension officer for advice.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1], "answerable": false, "qtype": "out_of_scope", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": null, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-o05", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": null, "latency_s": 7.536564499998349, "cost_usd": 0.00817175, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1808, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1391, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1319}, "total_tokens": 3199}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not give the maize price for this month. The price of maize can vary considerably depending on the location and the time of the year [S1]. Prices change during the year and from place to place [S3]. Contact your local extension officer for the current price.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 3], "answerable": false, "qtype": "out_of_scope", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": null, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-o06", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": null, "latency_s": 5.052676299994346, "cost_usd": 0.00591235, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1893, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 860, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 823}, "total_tokens": 2753}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not name a hybrid maize variety. Please contact your local extension officer for advice for your area.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [], "answerable": false, "qtype": "out_of_scope", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": null, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-o07", "split": "dev", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": null, "latency_s": 7.190753300004872, "cost_usd": 0.0072791, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2184, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1096, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1045}, "total_tokens": 3280}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not say what disease rots stalks at the base. They only describe Fall Armyworm. Please contact your local extension officer. [S2][S4]", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [2, 4], "answerable": false, "qtype": "out_of_scope", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": null, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
{"id": "q-o08", "split": "test", "setup": "cloud", "task": "qa", "retrieval_fact_hit": null, "latency_s": 10.076024699999834, "cost_usd": 0.00918135, "cached": false, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1880, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 99}, "output_tokens": 1633, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1572}, "total_tokens": 3513}, "supported": false, "answer_shown": "The passages do not tell how to control leaf beetles. They describe Fall Armyworm [S1] [S4] and stemborer damage [S1] [S2]. Contact your local extension officer for help.", "removed_sentences": [], "cited": [1, 2, 4], "answerable": false, "qtype": "out_of_scope", "invented_quantity": false, "auto_correct": true, "facts_hit": null, "correct": true, "graded_by": "auto"}
